## Key Concepts

- TensorFlow is a tool used for machine learning.
- Neural networks use layers of connected nodes.
- Each input can have a different weight.
- Training changes the weights to improve the model.
- Models need training data before they can make useful predictions.
- More training does not always mean better results.
- Machine learning can run locally on normal computers and phones.
- AI is used for things like image processing, speech recognition, and predictions.

## What is TensorFlow?

TensorFlow is a machine learning library.

It can be used to build and train neural networks. These networks take in data, process it through different layers, and produce an output.

The class also showed that TensorFlow can run on different devices, including computers, phones, and web browsers.

